macqd700-soc — licensing
========================

Original project contributions are offered under the MIT License below.
The project also includes third-party components under their own licenses.
This grant does not replace third-party licenses or grant rights we do not
hold. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for attribution and component-specific terms.

Ethernet-enabled bitstreams are subject to CERN-OHL-S-2.0. Component notices,
source obligations, and separate firmware/vendor-IP terms still apply.

MAME excerpts/adaptations retain BSD-3-Clause terms and credited authors.
Taxi Ethernet retains CERN-OHL-S-2.0, including its applicable source and
notice obligations. For combined designs incorporating Taxi, this project's
original contributions are additionally offered under CERN-OHL-S-2.0;
its complete text is in vendor/rk5-eth/third_party/taxi/LICENSE.
Disabling Ethernet does not remove obligations for other third-party code.

The cpu040 submodule has its own MIT contributions and third-party terms,
including SoftFloat Release 2b adaptations. Do not describe the entire
recursive checkout or generated hardware as exclusively MIT.

The VIA implementation drew inspiration from Shachar Shemesh’s CompuSAR/6522 project.

Apple firmware is not supplied in source Git. The next release bitstream
will also exclude the ADB modem firmware. Users insert their own ROM into
the blank bitstream locally; see docs/adb_firmware_bitstream.md.
Firmware is not covered by this project's licenses. FPGA vendor IP is
separately licensed as well.


